# shared object binaries
# NOTE: Likely will not need this, added just in case I include a package with C/C++ code.
# Would not want to forget to add later on...
*.so

# Stores bytecode
__pycache__/

## python compiled bytecode (.pyc) files shouldn't exist outside of __pycache__, but included just in case
## a misconfiguration occurs somewhere down the line.
*.pyc

###
# NOTE:
# .pyo (optimized bytecode) was deprecated after version 3.5; some guides suggest ignoring it anyway.
# .pyd (python dynamic library) files are exclusive to windows; unix-based systems use shared object binaries.
# (?) Sometimes windows uses .dll.

# If you want to cover all bases, uncomment below and comment line 6. (I just hate including unnecessary code.)
# *.py[cod]